{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791102042,"nonce":"Pn/qkx0i4/t07xWKDGu5kxjhf+k=","title":"Tw text classes on a box do not reach the text inside it","message":"`\u003cp class=\"text-xl font-bold text-text-secondary\"\u003eTitle\u003c/p\u003e` draws the text at the UA `p` size, weight and colour. Tw (and `style=`) set FontSize/FontWeight/TextColor as own props of the `p` box, but Css.apply only passes inherited values (`INHERITED`, `--*`) from the parent's applied CSS values, so a Tw-set font property on an element never reaches its text children. A stylesheet rule on the same element does inherit.\n\nReproducer: tools/snapshot/scenes/ComponentsGallery.hx before it was moved to a page sheet; any `\u003cp class=\"text-sm\"\u003e`.\n\nExpected: Tailwind's behaviour — `text-*`, `font-*`, `leading-*`, `tracking-*`, `text-\u003ccolour\u003e` and `text-left|center|right|justify` on an element apply to the text it holds, as inherited CSS properties do. Likely route: the inherited text props Tw/`style=` set on a non-text element enter the cascade as that element's own (inline-layer) values, so children inherit them.","files":null}]}